Subject: [PATCH 099/191] [ae-patch] Pick the Claude account when forking a
 Claude session

Upstream v0.17.0 retired in-place agent switching
(https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/pull/8795), and with it the way a
running Claude session moved to another of the host's Claude subscription
accounts (patch 0067). Reid asked on 2026-10-18 for that choice to live in the
fork dialog instead. The fork request takes claude_account; the server checks
it against the source host's detected Claude logins with the rules the switch
route used (ae_fork_claude_account.py) and stamps omnigent.claude_native.account
through the fork's extra labels, which the runner reads at Claude launch. The
dialog's run-config section shows a Claude account row for a Claude native
fork that stays on the source session's host. openapi.json is regenerated.
